atlas commands-fabric-owner

architecture dual-agent-fabric-native-owner
  canonical_name DualAgentFabricNativeOwner
  family commands
  domain Execution / Durable cross-agent work and isolated convergence
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Can independent agent proposals, isolated implementation and evidence-gated application share one durable cancellable work owner without turning model output into authority?
  purpose Replace the Python broker with Bun scheduling and the existing real agent CLIs while preserving fourteen tools, four prompts, task handles, sessions, events and receipt identities.
  node_types DurableTask
  node_types AgentRun
  node_types IsolatedWorktree
  node_types SourceSnapshot
  node_types LaneLock
  node_types ReviewVerdict
  node_types PatchReceipt
  node_types TaskDisclosureAdmission
  node_types RecipientNotification
  node_types ReviewedAccountModelTask
  node_types NativeUsageReceipt
  node_types RecipientPushAttempt
  internal_calculus bounded admission -> atomic queued task claim -> optional exact-hash current-source admission -> pinned isolated baseline -> owned process groups -> early Project patch admission -> review and conditional repair -> executable tests and one bounded test repair -> concurrent independent final verification -> unchanged patch identity -> fresh Project preview and guarded apply
  internal_calculus cancellation -> terminal cancellation state -> terminate owned subprocess groups -> join -> release lane locks
  internal_calculus trusted native actor and destination admission -> immutable task scope in existing Fabric SQLite -> current process execution witness -> bounded MessagePack activity -> recipient revision and request receipt for read or dismiss
  internal_calculus fresh native write authority -> exact local model and pricing review -> synchronous scoped task and request receipt -> existing bounded queue -> pinned native lease and physical attempt -> retained output -> native Meter event -> recipient attention
  invariant restart does not replay historical queued or running work; recorded running state is not evidence of a surviving process
  invariant cancelled tasks cannot become successful when a late subprocess result arrives; foreign lock expiry does not prove executor death
  invariant agent dispatch tools are effects despite inherited readOnlyHint annotations; task submission obeys STOP and bounded scheduling
  invariant untracked additions are included in isolated worktree patches; reviewed patch changes invalidate application
  invariant Project MCP owns live patch authority; ambiguous apply responses remain uncertain and are never automatically retried
  invariant Project reads and patch operations use the configured Project endpoint independently of the mesh endpoint; remote Project placement requires a dedicated credential
  invariant known Project preflight refusals stop before review expense, failed tests receive at most one configured repair in the same worktree, and persistent failures never enter final verification or apply
  invariant repair may be skipped only for a structured review with resolved state, nonempty evidence and no blocking findings; both independent final verdicts and successful tests remain required for apply
  invariant compact task reads omit prompts, agent output and receipt bodies; live executor ownership and queue position come from the service process, never from a historical running row
  invariant legacy unbound tasks remain operator work; account disclosure is admitted atomically with task creation and cannot be added or reassigned later
  invariant task disclosure follows the native subject and scope; notification lifecycle additionally matches the current recipient actor and never cancels or resumes work
  invariant the internal activity carrier accepts only authenticated native exact operations and rejects browser origins; reviewed account model execution has a separate fresh native write and exact-model admission path and cannot dispatch operator tools
  invariant model work shares the existing Fabric queue STOP capacity and cancellation owners; legacy MCP dispatch cannot select model kind or supply account disclosure coordinates
  invariant a physical model attempt is retained before inference; restart cancellation or an incomplete response cannot cause automatic replay
  invariant Meter repair uses the retained exact attempt output bytes duration and identity; a lost native acknowledgement cannot create a second inference or a second usage event
  invariant current native Auth and CMS access is checked at model dispatch and recipient push delivery; stored scope and browser permission are not substitute authority
  invariant local output verification resolves immutable bytes through the model owner and fresh initiating-account permission; peer claims never become account or remote recipient authority
  invariant optional source_files admit at most sixty-four explicit regular files or absent paths and eight MiB total; stale hashes, unsafe paths, ignored files and cancelled preparation refuse before agent execution
  invariant selected source is retained as a hashed receipt and isolated Git baseline without changing the project HEAD or index; baseline diffs exclude supplied inputs and remain pinned if an agent commits
  invariant baseline object hashing uses one no-filter batch and one index-info update; Git object identities are compared with captured bytes and repository attributes that reinterpret the baseline refuse admission
  invariant selected source hashes and modes are checked again before apply; detected source changes retain the candidate for review and never relax Project clean-path or write policy
  forbidden_inference admitted selected source -> complete dependency coverage, an atomic repository snapshot, or authority to write a dirty path
  forbidden_inference passing CLI exit or model-authored JSON -> correctness of the proposed patch, independent proof, or permission to bypass Project authority
  forbidden_inference child environment peer depth -> authenticated recursion isolation across MCP HTTP clients sharing a credential
  forbidden_inference local contract and fixture tests -> live paid-provider behavior, estate-wide performance, or complete retirement of all Python services
  forbidden_inference destination membership or a notification dismissal -> task execution authority, recipient fan-out, cancellation, or permission to disclose an unbound task
  forbidden_inference a retained receipt digest and kind -> a safe artifact body or a downloadable file
